RUBEN KRUIT: Fully agree, yeah.

00:40:39.470 --> 00:40:41.710
I think the other question
is pretty important.

00:40:41.710 --> 00:40:44.250
Why is there so little
promotion for G Suite?

00:40:44.250 --> 00:40:44.800
BAS ROOKHUIJZEN:
That's a good one.

00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:46.690
We're a well-hidden
secret in that sense.

00:40:46.690 --> 00:40:46.910
RUBEN KRUIT: Yeah.

00:40:46.910 --> 00:40:47.826
BAS ROOKHUIJZEN: Yeah.

00:40:47.826 --> 00:40:49.630
So Google is a
technology company.

00:40:49.630 --> 00:40:52.470
We're not that
good in marketing.

00:40:52.470 --> 00:40:54.670
You won't see us a lot in
the [INAUDIBLE] dot-blots,

00:40:54.670 --> 00:40:56.920
or at the--

00:40:56.920 --> 00:40:58.810
so we like to be
relevant and we like

00:40:58.810 --> 00:41:02.390
to be found the moment that
you think it's relevant.

00:41:02.390 --> 00:41:04.197
So it's in the nature of Google.

00:41:04.197 --> 00:41:06.280
We don't make a lot of
advertisement on Google.com

00:41:06.280 --> 00:41:08.950
or Androids either.

00:41:08.950 --> 00:41:11.787
We just want to have happy users
communicate it to each other.

00:41:11.787 --> 00:41:13.870
RUBEN KRUIT: Yeah, well I
can add something to it.

00:41:13.870 --> 00:41:17.320
Because OK, it's maybe not
that visual in the promotion.

00:41:17.320 --> 00:41:21.500
But on the other hand, once
you are in contact with Google,

00:41:21.500 --> 00:41:23.650
they have a very, very
interesting program

00:41:23.650 --> 00:41:28.750
for companies to make sure
that you get on their tools,

00:41:28.750 --> 00:41:32.200
get on their applications very
smoothly, also by providing

00:41:32.200 --> 00:41:34.360
vouchers for the
transition costs,

00:41:34.360 --> 00:41:38.140
for instance, or being very
creative in, well let's say,

00:41:38.140 --> 00:41:40.150
when your first
license bill is going

00:41:40.150 --> 00:41:45.440
to end up on the
[INAUDIBLE] of your company.

00:41:45.440 --> 00:41:48.250
So therefore, yeah, I think
that's a different way

00:41:48.250 --> 00:41:54.610
of promoting that's getting
people to want your product,

00:41:54.610 --> 00:41:57.670
instead of pushing your
product, but making it very easy

00:41:57.670 --> 00:42:02.185
for you to do that
transition to that product.

00:42:02.185 --> 00:42:03.310
BAS ROOKHUIJZEN: Thank you.

00:42:03.310 --> 00:42:05.110
So another interesting
thing is how do you

00:42:05.110 --> 00:42:07.960
secure mobile devices in terms
of remote management and policy

00:42:07.960 --> 00:42:08.630
provisioning?

00:42:08.630 --> 00:42:10.004
So we have two
products for that.

00:42:10.004 --> 00:42:12.440
Within G Suite embedded is
mobile device management

00:42:12.440 --> 00:42:12.940
already.

00:42:12.940 --> 00:42:15.250
So you can enroll all
your mobile devices

00:42:15.250 --> 00:42:16.680
that you want, also iPhones.

00:42:16.680 --> 00:42:17.830
It doesn't matter.

00:42:17.830 --> 00:42:20.170
Android devices, you'll have
way more settings than we

00:42:20.170 --> 00:42:23.050
deploy in iPhones in our suite.

00:42:23.050 --> 00:42:25.090
But it's still possible.

00:42:25.090 --> 00:42:27.190
On top of that, we
have Android for Work.

00:42:27.190 --> 00:42:28.970
And that's mobile
application management.

00:42:28.970 --> 00:42:31.210
And you can also
push applications,

00:42:31.210 --> 00:42:33.640
and the beauty of
it is that other

00:42:33.640 --> 00:42:36.670
than the usual mobile
application management suites

00:42:36.670 --> 00:42:39.730
that you can buy today,
those are containerized.

00:42:39.730 --> 00:42:41.611
Meaning that once
you're in the container,

00:42:41.611 --> 00:42:43.360
you can access all the
information, right?

00:42:43.360 --> 00:42:45.930
So what we've done we have
tunnels to those applications.

00:42:45.930 --> 00:42:48.554
So the applications are just in
between the normal applications

00:42:48.554 --> 00:42:50.190
in the phone of the user.

00:42:50.190 --> 00:42:52.300
And we have added a
little icon to it.

00:42:52.300 --> 00:42:54.940
So it's the icon of a suitcase.

00:42:54.940 --> 00:42:57.040
And that enables
you, as a company

00:42:57.040 --> 00:42:58.430
to communicate it to the user.

00:42:58.430 --> 00:42:59.680
That's very easy to recognize.

00:42:59.680 --> 00:43:03.010
Those apps are
company policy pushed.

00:43:03.010 --> 00:43:05.890
And those apps I just
download WhatsApp,

00:43:05.890 --> 00:43:08.860
whatever the user uses
itself, to himself or herself.

00:43:08.860 --> 00:43:10.100
He can just deploy it.

00:43:10.100 --> 00:43:12.490
So it's mobile application
management and mobile device

00:43:12.490 --> 00:43:13.300
management.

00:43:13.300 --> 00:43:16.210
Second advantage is that also
because of this tunneling,

00:43:16.210 --> 00:43:18.010
you don't need to
wrap the app anymore.

00:43:18.010 --> 00:43:20.320
Third-party apps are
really hard to wrap.

00:43:20.320 --> 00:43:22.600
The moment that you want
to put it into a container

00:43:22.600 --> 00:43:26.380
that we used that we are
used to working with today,

00:43:26.380 --> 00:43:28.930
if you just put them in
the Google App Store,

00:43:28.930 --> 00:43:31.960
you create your own Google
App Store for your company.

00:43:31.960 --> 00:43:35.080
And then you can push any
app, also all third-party apps

00:43:35.080 --> 00:43:36.350
available.

00:43:36.350 --> 00:43:38.350
So I hope-- if you have
any specific question,

00:43:38.350 --> 00:43:41.310
just contact me.

00:43:41.310 --> 00:43:42.310
Then there's a question.

00:43:42.310 --> 00:43:42.670
Who are you?

00:43:42.670 --> 00:43:44.680
But I put that in there
to check if that's right.

